0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, SEPTEMBER 9, 2009\r\rMayor Wolfson called the meeting to order at 7:06 p.m. in the City Council Chambers, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Wolfson, Mayor pro Tem Groveman, Councilmembers Bozajian, Maurer and Washburn.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Bartlett, Cohen, Colantuono, Coroalles, Peirce, Yalda.\r \r The Pledge of Allegiance was led by Noah Palm. \r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r \r Councilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Washburn to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS\r\rMayor Wolfson presented proclamations to the members of Boys In Action in recognition of their community service work. Mayor Wolfson announced that the final Sunset Series Concert will be occurring on Sunday, September 13 at Calabasas Lake and spoke regarding the upcoming Calabasas Pumpkin Festival on October 17-18, 2009.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT:\r\r No one indicated a desire to speak.\r\rCONSENT ITEMS \r\r Approval of meeting minutes from August 26, 2009.\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2009-1207, establishing employee flex credit amounts for 2010 and rescinding Resolution No. 2009-1158. \r\r Authorization to approve additional annual funding for Valleycrest Landscape Maintenance in the amount of $41,500 for the 2009-2010 fiscal year budget to perform required irrigation system repair and damaged plant material replacement as part of Specification No. 07-08-06 landscape maintenance of public works street medians, certain sidewalks and parkway areas.\r\r Approval of a city-county law enforcement services Agreement with the Los Angeles County Sheriff�s Department from September 1, 2009 through June 30, 2014. \rCouncilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to approve Consent Items 1, 2, 3, and 4. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rPUBLIC HEARING\r\r Adoption of Resolution No. 2009-1204, approving a fee schedule for Onsite Waste Water Treatment System (OWTS) Operating permit program. \r\rMayor Wolfson opened the public hearing.\r\rTom Bartlett, City Planner, and Sparky Cohen, Building Official, presented the staff report.\r\rMayor Wolfson closed the public hearing.\r\r Councilmember Washburn moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Groveman, to adopt Resolution No. 2009-1204, approving a fee schedule for Onsite Waste Water Treatment System (OWTS) Operating permit program with direction to waive the fee for permits pulled in the first six months. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rUNFINISHED BUSINESS \r\r Discussion regarding options for funding for Onsite Waste Water Treatment System (OWTS) inspections.\r\rTom Bartlett, City Planner, and Sparky Cohen, Building Official, presented the staff report.\r\rJody Thomas, Calabasas, Richard Thompson, Calabasas, spoke in support of a full subsidy for inspections. Helene Regan, Calabasas, Robert Pope, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to using public funds to subsidize private property.\r\rThe City Council provided direction to staff on a grant program for lower income residents and requested that a report with the median income for Calabasas residents be presented to Council at a future meeting.\r\r Discussion regarding feasibility of sewer expansion in Old Topanga.\r\rAnita Davidoo, Associate Engineer, presented the staff report.\r\rJody Thomas, Calabasas, Toby Keeler, Calabasas, Russ Sutherland, Calabasas, Jenna Mitchell, Calabasas, spoke in opposition to proposed sewer expansion in Old Topanga. \r\rA majority of the City Council provided direction to staff to move forward with putting out a Request for Proposal for an Environmental Impact Report on sewer expansion in Old Topanga. Councilmembers Bozajian and Maurer opposed.\rNEW BUSINESS \r\r Introduction of Ordinance No. 2009-263, adopting the 2008 California Green Building Standards Code, Part 11 of the California Code of Regulations Title 24 with local amendments. \r\rSparky Cohen, Building Official, presented the staff report.\r\r Mayor pro Tem Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Bozajian, to introduce Ordinance No. 2009-263, adopting the 2008 California Green Building Standards Code, Part 11 of the California Code of Regulations Title 24 with local amendments. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rINFORMATIONAL REPORTS\r\r Check Register for the period of August 18, 2009 to August 26, 2009. \r\r There was no action taken.\r\rTASK FORCE REPORTS \r\r Councilmember Maurer provided a report from a recent School Area Task Force Meeting.\r\rCITY MANAGER�S REPORT \r\r City Manager Coroalles indicated he had nothing to report.\r\rFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS \r\r Councilmember Washburn requested an item be placed on a future agenda regarding the City participating in the �Complete Census� program.\r\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015ADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 9:35 p.m. in memory of Fred Williams to the next regularly scheduled meeting on Wednesday, September 23, 2009 at 7:00 p.m.\r\r\r\r\r\r__________________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC, City Clerk\r\r\r\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00142\u0015\r\r\r\u0013 PAGE \\* MERGEFORMAT \u00142\u0015\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u00